# `integration/ebiten`

`golem-ebiten` publishes Ebiten helpers for Golem Engine clients. It depends on `golem-go-client` as the protocol/client runtime and should not duplicate Go transport, protobuf, or generated-manager behavior.

The `ebiten` codegen integration emits raw `.go` bridge scaffolds from `codegen/templates/ebiten/`. There is intentionally no compile finalizer here; the consumer game module compiles bridge files alongside game code.

`Game` owns client lifecycle for Ebiten loops: connect during setup, reconnect unexpected drops with backoff from `Update`, and disconnect on shutdown. It accepts either credential-free `ConnectionPlan` / `ConnectionPlanProvider` inputs or legacy `ConnectOptions`; precedence is plan provider, static plan, legacy options provider, then static options. A plan is one lifecycle attempt, so transport fallback does not consume reconnect backoff. Per-dial credentials belong in the plan resolver, while the plan provider refreshes only credential-free endpoint configuration. Connection completion is generation-fenced so a disconnect reported during a physical connect keeps its reconnect schedule and suppresses the stale connect callback. Provider errors cross the public/logging boundary through opaque wrappers that preserve `errors.Is` / `errors.As` without exposing ticket-bearing text. `ConnectedTransport` reports the physical transport selected by the Go client. Keep the helper independent of a specific generated package so games can embed it in their own `ebiten.Game`.

Generated bridges embed `Synced<Name>` from the `go-client` protocol output. Preserve the hook contract: `OnSpawn` creates drawables, `OnRemove` destroys the optional drawable, `ApplyState`/`ApplyDelta` call the embedded synced state before `SyncToDrawable`, and entity event hooks are named `On<Name>`.

Rendering helpers should stay thin and optional. Generated views may expose a `Drawable` and `Positioned` contract, but game-specific animation, camera logic, and asset ownership should remain in the consumer game unless a helper is broadly reusable.

When changing Ebiten bridge shapes, update codegen template tests and runtime tests under `golem-ebiten/`.
